p.src:
A general pure state of the pair is $\ket\Psi
  =
  c_{uu}\ket{uu}
  +c_{du}\ket{du}
  +c_{ud}\ket{ud}
  +c_{dd}\ket{dd}.$ Four complex coefficients give eight real numbers. Normalization removes one and overall phase removes one: $8-1-1=6.$ A separately prepared pure state of electron $1$ needs two real parameters, and electron $2$ needs two more, for only four. The two missing parameters are not an accounting error. They signal pure states of the pair that cannot be assigned separate pure states for the parts.

