p.src:
First identify the states that do come from separate preparations. If $\ket{\psi_1}=\alpha_1\ket u+\beta_1\ket d,
  \qquad
  \ket{\psi_2}=\alpha_2\ket u+\beta_2\ket d,$ then $\begin{aligned}
  \ket{\psi_1}\otimes\ket{\psi_2}
  &=
  \alpha_1\alpha_2\ket{uu}
  +\alpha_1\beta_2\ket{ud}
  \notag\\
  &\quad
  +\beta_1\alpha_2\ket{du}
  +\beta_1\beta_2\ket{dd}.
  \end{aligned}$ This is a product state. Each electron has its own polarization axis, just as it would if the two magnetic preparations were performed independently.

