p.src:
To see what either electron looks like alone, calculate the three local expectation values. For the first component, $\sigma_1\ket{\psi_+}
  =
  \frac{1}{\sqrt2}
  \left(\ket{dd}+\ket{uu}\right),$ which is orthogonal to $\ket{\psi_+}$. Therefore $\bra{\psi_+}\sigma_1\ket{\psi_+}=0.$ Similarly, $\sigma_2\ket{\psi_+}
  =
  \frac{i}{\sqrt2}
  \left(\ket{dd}-\ket{uu}\right),$ so $\bra{\psi_+}\sigma_2\ket{\psi_+}=0.$ For the third component, $\sigma_3\ket{\psi_+}
  =
  \frac{1}{\sqrt2}
  \left(\ket{ud}-\ket{du}\right),$ and the two diagonal contributions cancel: $\bra{\psi_+}\sigma_3\ket{\psi_+}
  =\frac12(1-1)=0.$ Thus $\begin{aligned}
    \bra{\psi_+}\sigma_i\ket{\psi_+}&=0,\\
    \bra{\psi_+}\tau_i\ket{\psi_+}&=0,
    \qquad i=1,2,3.
  \end{aligned}$

